WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.530
- I think that we have
a clip of this though.

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:03.450
We have to see this. Okay, show it.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.920
- [Anna] Never know when
you're gonna get stuck

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.180
in an elevator.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.685
Did you say "open up the hatch"?

00:00:07.685 --> 00:00:08.910
- [Speaker] Yeah.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.080
- [Anna] Everybody watch your head.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.470
- [Speaker] I can't
believe this is happening.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:13.710
Are you (beep) kidding me?

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.153
- Go!
- Come on, we got ya.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.353
- It's a good thing I'm not
wearing a short skirt today.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.510
I know! It was-
- This is my worst nightmare.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:22.830
You're obviously in an elevator.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.480
- Yeah, so we got stuck in an elevator.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.270
This is the first day of press
at the Toronto Film Festival

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.670
for "Alice, Darling."

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.590
Yeah, a bunch of us got
stuck in an elevator.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.240
And at first, the elevator jolts

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.107
and you all make a little joke about like,

00:00:35.107 --> 00:00:38.136
"Can you imagine if we got
trapped in this elevator?"

00:00:38.136 --> 00:00:41.517
And then it was like I was in "Die Hard."

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.590
They pull you. 'Cause I thought-

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:44.940
- Great Christmas film.
- Yes.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.687
Even though they call the
fire department, you're like,

00:00:46.687 --> 00:00:49.110
"Oh, they're gonna pry open
the doors or something."

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.270
But we were actually stuck between floors

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.230
and we had to do the thing

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.300
of getting pulled up through the hatch.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.530
It was very exciting.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.290
It was the most action
star thing I've ever done.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:01.590
- [Kelly] Is this before
or after your press day?

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.650
- This is before. This was like
at the beginning of the day.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.530
So I sat down to start
doing the first press junket

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.363
for "Alice, Darling,"

00:01:08.363 --> 00:01:10.920
and every journalist that
came in to interview me,

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.120
I was like, "Oh, I'm so sorry I'm late,

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.220
I was just stuck in this
elevator," and da-da-da.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.577
And all of them just thought like,

00:01:15.577 --> 00:01:18.390
"Oh, Anna's funny, so she's doing a bit."

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.730
And the more that I was like,
"No, you don't understand,

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:24.090
I literally just now got
pulled out of the ceiling

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:26.700
of the thing, of the
elevator, by firefighters."

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.087
And they're like, "She is so funny.

00:01:30.087 --> 00:01:32.767
She is really committed to
this bit. She is too funny."

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:35.370
- "You can just say you're
late, girl." (laughs)

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:38.070
Oh my God. That's my worst
nightmare, by the way.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.660
And I always make that joke when I go in,

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.103
just so it won't happen.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:45.420
That's what I literally do
to just trip up the universe.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.770
Like, "Oh, wouldn't it
be funny if it happened?"

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.180
and then it doesn't.
- Well, it didn't work for me.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:51.130
- Yeah, it didn't work for you.
I shall not say it anymore.

